    "doi": "https://doi.org/10.1038/nclimate1958",
    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Climate change impacts on marine ecosystems",
    "problem": "Past meta-analyses on the response of marine life to climate change have been limited in their geographic, taxonomic, and biological scope, which has precluded a robust and comprehensive global overview of the consistency and magnitude of climate-driven impacts in the ocean.",
    "method": "To provide a robust overview of climate change effects on marine life, this study synthesized 1,735 observations from 208 peer-reviewed papers into a meta-database, evaluating the consistency of observed ecological responses with expectations under climate change and quantifying the rates of distribution and phenology shifts.",
    "task": "The task is to synthesize all available studies on marine life to determine if observed ecological responses are consistent with the expected impacts of climate change, thereby providing a robust overview of its global effects on the oceans.",
